Modifications made to the original icons (Apache License 2.0, section 4(b)):
- path coordinates rescaled from viewBox "0 -960 960 960" to "0 0 24 24"
  (same geometry, no redrawing)
- degenerate helper subpaths with zero area removed
- each icon split into parts (outline plus its holes) and animated
- output in two formats: animated SVG (SMIL) and Android
  AnimatedVectorDrawable XML, each in a loop and a one-shot variant
- battery_20, battery_30, battery_50, battery_60, battery_80, battery_90:
  the upstream 24px export of these icons lost its charge-level layer and
  draws a full battery. Their drawing is rebuilt from battery_0_bar of the
  same set (same outline) with the interior hole ending at the stated
  charge (tools/make_source_fixes.py, folder source_fixes)
- "_off" and "_disabled" icons made from index 621 on (for example
  cloud_off): while the slash moves, the matching icon of the same set (for
  example cloud) is drawn, clipped, in the area the slash leaves; at rest
  only the original icon is drawn. The file comment names the icon used.
  car_seat_off has no matching icon in the set: a seated person drawn for
  this project is used in the same way.
- icons made from index 621 on whose drawing is a single shape (for example
  call_made or cloud_upload): while moving, the path is drawn as clipped
  pieces (for example the head and the shaft of an arrow); at rest only the
  original path is drawn. The file comment says so.
- clock_loader_10 ... clock_loader_90: while the wedge moves, two clipped
  copies of the same path are drawn in place of it; at rest only the
  original path is drawn.
Every modified file carries a comment stating its origin and the changes.

The generator used for the icons from index 621 on is in tools/m3a
(Copyright 2026 Marco Morosi, Apache License, Version 2.0). It reads the
Material Symbols sources, which are not included in its folder.

